pes dining_table_1 with cloth_1, the robot wipes mirror_1 with cloth_2.","level":1,"path_id":"1~67","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":70,"section_id":"sec-1~67"},{"title":"↩→ ↩→","text":"Additional information from the user","level":1,"path_id":"1~68","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":71,"section_id":"sec-1~68"},{"title":"GPT-4: Wipe a surface","text":"Parameters: 1. ?x -furnitureAppliance: the furniture or appliance to be wiped and cleaned 2. ?c -householdObject: the cloth to be used for wiping and cleaningPreconditions: (and (robot-at ?x) (robot-holding ?c) (washable ?c) (object-washed ?c) Incorrect precondition: ?x doesn't need to have a flat surface (flat-surface ?x) Missing precondition: ?c should be a cloth ) Effects: (and (not (object-washed ?c)) (object-dirty ?c) (furniture-cleaned ?x) ) A.6.22 Vacuum a carpet","level":1,"path_id":"1~69","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":72,"section_id":"sec-1~69"},{"title":"Action description","text":"This action enables the robot to vacuum a carpet with a handheld vacuum cleaner. For example, the robot uses vacuum_cleaner_1 to vacuum carpet_2, the robot uses vacuum_cleaner_2 to vacuum carpet_1.","level":1,"path_id":"1~70","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":73,"section_id":"sec-1~70"},{"title":"↩→ ↩→","text":"Additional information from the user (a) You need to make sure the dust bin of the vacuum cleaner is not full before executing this action.↩→ (b) You may assume the robot is holding the vacuum cleaner at the beginning. (c) The dust bin of the vacuum cleaner will be full of dust.","level":1,"path_id":"1~71","parent_section_id":null,"order_in_parent":74,"section_id":"sec-1~71"},{"title":"GPT4: Vacuum a carpet","text":"Parameters: 1. ?v -householdObject: the handheld vacuum cleaner to use 2. ?c -furnitureAppliance: the carpet to vacuum Preconditions: (and (robot-holding ?v) (robot-at ?c) (pickupable ?v) (not (dustbin-full ?v)) (not (carpet-clean ?c)) Missing precondition: ?v should be a 